Runtime: Memory Model

Purpose:
  Define the 4-tier memory hierarchy and TMP memory for AI working memory.
  Memory tiers govern what knowledge is loaded, retained, and promoted
  across task executions, optimizing token usage and preserving engineering
  truth at the appropriate persistence level.

Principles:
  Working memory is runtime-only and never persisted to .sdd/.
  TMP memory is transient for external analysis only.
  Memory promotion is evidence-driven, not assumed.
  AI remembers decisions, not conversations.
  Token budget is optimized by loading only relevant memory tier content.

MemoryTiers:
  LongTermKnowledge:
    definition: permanent engineering truth
    scope: cross-project, survives project deletion
    examples:
      - @best-practice.solid
      - @best-practice.kiss
      - @ddd.aggregate
      - @architecture.hexagonal
      - @security.password-hashing
    schema:
      id: canonical reference
      type: concept | pattern | skill
      status: established
      trust: proven
      evidence_count: integer
      projects_used: integer
      tasks_referenced: integer
    ttl: indefinite
    importance_rating: critical | high | normal | low | temporary
    persistence: permanent

  ProjectMemory:
    definition: project-specific knowledge
    scope: single project lifecycle
    examples:
      - @project.payment (PostgreSQL, modular-monolith, RabbitMQ, JWT)
      - @project.api-gateway
    schema:
      id: canonical reference
      project: project_id
      type: architecture | decision | constraint | skill
      status: active | deprecated
      trust: validated
      evidence:
        - task_id
        - decision_id
        - test_result
    ttl: project lifetime
    importance_rating: critical | high | normal | low | temporary
    persistence: project-scoped

  TaskMemory:
    definition: current task knowledge
    scope: active task execution only
    examples:
      - TASK-1023: implement wallet withdrawal
      - relevant: @payment.idempotency, @wallet.aggregate
      - decisions: @decision.atomic-balance-update
    schema:
      task_id: string
      goal: string
      relevant:
        - reference_id
      decisions:
        - decision_id
      status: active | completed
    ttl: task lifetime
    importance_rating: critical | high | normal | low | temporary
    persistence: task-scoped

  WorkingMemory:
    definition: current reasoning context
    scope: single task execution iteration
    examples:
      - file: wallet.go
      - problem: balance mutation
      - constraints: atomic, idempotent
      - candidate: transaction + aggregate lock
    schema:
      current:
        file: string
        problem: string
        constraints: list
      candidate: string
      observation: string
      insight: string
    ttl: task execution iteration
    importance_rating: critical | high | normal | low | temporary
    persistence: runtime-only, never persisted to .sdd/

   TmpMemory:
    definition: external material and temporary analysis
    scope: transient analysis, never part of project knowledge
    schema:
      source: external | scratch
      content: string
      analysis: string
    ttl: immediate (end of reasoning step)
    importance_rating: temporary
    persistence: runtime-only, never persisted

  RuntimeBridge:
    definition: Maps .sdd memory tiers to claude-mem physical stores
    source: thedotmack/claude-mem SessionStore.ts + analysis-comprehensive.md
    stores:
      SQLite:
        tier: TaskMemory + ProjectMemory metadata
        schema: 49 migrations, SHA-256 content_hash, FTS5 for full-text
        location: ~/.claude-mem.db (per-user)
        role: primary metadata store for session_id, content_session_id, observations
        dedup: SHA-256 content-hash, ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING

      ChromaDB:
        tier: LongTermKnowledge (semantic layer)
        schema: vector embeddings (text-embedding-3-small)
        location: Chroma server (default localhost:8000)
        role: semantic search with tier routing
        dedup: same as SQLite (content_hash foreign key)

      SHA-256_HashStore:
        tier: All tiers (dedup key)
        schema: content_hash as primary key
        role: cross-store dedup, integrity verification
        note: Prevents duplicate observations from multiple harness hooks

    PersistenceMapping:
      LongTermKnowledge -> ChromaDB (semantic) + SQLite (metadata)
      ProjectMemory -> SQLite (primary) + ChromaDB (semantic index)
      TaskMemory -> SQLite (per-execution tables) + in-memory cache
      WorkingMemory -> runtime-only (never persisted)
      TmpMemory -> runtime-only (never persisted)

    RecallMechanism:
      tier_routing: filter -> ChromaDB semantic -> FTS5 fallback
      recency_gate: 90-day window (configurable via CLAUDE_MEM_MAX_RECALL_AGE)
      token_budget: progressive disclosure (metadata first ~100 tokens,
        instructions < 5000 tokens, resources on demand)
      sanitization: L0 sanitize step before injection (prompt-injection prevention)
      hot_cold: hot (referenced ≥50% recent) loaded by default, cold (not
        referenced 90 days) loaded on demand only

    Consolidation:
      ratio: 100 runtime events -> ~3 decisions + 1 new skill
      source: .sdd/runtime/memory-consolidation.sdd
      hot_classification: referenced in ≥50% of recent tasks in last 14 days
      cold_classification: not referenced in 90 days
      storage: consolidated output stored to ProjectMemory / LongTermKnowledge

MemoryPromotionPipeline:
  stages:
    WORKING_MEMORY:
      description: active reasoning context
      next: OBSERVATION

    OBSERVATION:
      description: noticed pattern or fact without evidence
      next: INSIGHT

    INSIGHT:
      description: hypothesis or connection with some evidence
      next: CANDIDATE

    CANDIDATE:
      description: proposed knowledge awaiting validation
      ttl: 30 days (auto-expires to ARCHIVE if unvalidated)
      next: VALIDATED_KNOWLEDGE

    VALIDATED_KNOWLEDGE:
      description: confirmed by evidence, ready for promotion
      next: LONG_TERM_KNOWLEDGE

    LONG_TERM_KNOWLEDGE:
      description: permanent engineering truth
      persistence: permanent

  promotion_rules:
    - promotion requires evidence: CODE, TEST, TASK, DECISION, PROJECT, PRODUCTION, EXTERNAL, HUMAN
    - candidate without validation after 30 days is archived
    - validated knowledge may be promoted to long-term after project verification
    - project-specific knowledge does not auto-promote to long-term
    - trust hierarchy: explicit project constraints > decisions > validated project skills > established org knowledge > general best practices > AI suggestions

MemoryImportance:
  critical:
    description: security decisions, data integrity, architectural invariants
    examples:
      - @constitution.security
      - @constitution.data-integrity
    always_load: true

  high:
    description: core domain decisions, primary patterns
    examples:
      - @decision.rabbitmq
      - @payment.idempotency

  normal:
    description: supporting knowledge, secondary patterns
    examples:
      - @ddd.specification
      - @architecture.repository

  low:
    description: rarely used, historical, optional
    examples:
      - @legacy.payment-v1
    default_context: false

  temporary:
    description: debugging hypothesis, migration scratch, transient analysis
    examples:
      - @insight.current-migration
    ttl: task-lifetime or explicit expires

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  Context: @context.sdd
  Context Builder: @context-builder.sdd
  Context Policy: @context-policy.sdd
  Context Manifest: @context-manifest.sdd
  Memory Consolidation: @memory-consolidation.sdd
  Execution: @execution.sdd
  Agent: @../agent/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [RT-MM-01] Working memory is runtime-only and MUST NOT be persisted to .sdd/.
  [RT-MM-02] TMP memory is transient for external analysis only and MUST NOT be persisted.
  [RT-MM-03] Long-term knowledge survives project deletion; project memory does not.
  [RT-MM-04] Memory promotion is evidence-driven; candidates without validation expire after 30 days.
  [RT-MM-05] AI MUST remember decisions, not conversations.
  [RT-MM-06] Trust hierarchy: explicit project constraints > decisions > validated project skills > established org knowledge > general best practices > AI suggestions.
  [RT-MM-07] Memory importance rating determines default context inclusion.
  [RT-MM-08] Critical importance knowledge MUST be always loaded.
  [RT-MM-09] Low importance knowledge MUST NOT be in default context; loaded on demand only.
  [RT-MM-10] Temporary importance knowledge MUST have explicit TTL or task-lifetime bound.
  [RT-MM-11] Project memory does not auto-promote to long-term knowledge.
  [RT-MM-12] Memory consolidation occurs at end of each task execution.
  [RT-MM-13] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to memory outputs.
  [RT-MM-14] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in memory output headers or titles.

State: +
